idealFromShelling -- Produces an ideal from a shelling
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = idealFromShelling(P)
        I = idealFromShelling(S,P)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, (If omitted, it will use
        S=QQ[x_0..x_{n-1}] where n is the maximum integer in the lists of P.
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of lists of integers.
        Each list of integers is a facet of the complex and the order is a
        shelling.
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, (If omitted, it will use
        S=QQ[x_0..x_{n-1}] where n is the maximum integer in the lists of P.
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, generated by the monomials
        representing the minimal nonfaces of P

Description
===========

This gives the Stanley-Reisner ideal for the simplicial complex, that is the
ideal generated by the monomials representing the minimal nonfaces of P.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x_0,x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4]                       |
|                                                       |
|o1 = S                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P =  {{1, 2, 4}, {0, 1, 4}, {0, 2, 4}, {0, 3, 4}};|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : idealFromShelling(S,P)                            |
|                                                       |
|o3 = monomialIdeal (x x x , x x , x x )                |
|                     0 1 2   1 3   2 3                 |
|                                                       |
|o3 : MonomialIdeal of S                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

