regSeq -- regular sequence of powers of the variables, in given degrees
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = regSeq(L,S)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, or sequence of positive integers
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, Polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, generated by the given powers
        of the variables

Description
===========

+-----------------------+
|i1 : kk=ZZ/101         |
|                       |
|o1 = kk                |
|                       |
|o1 : QuotientRing      |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : S=kk[a..e]        |
|                       |
|o2 = S                 |
|                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : regSeq((2,3,4),S) |
|                       |
|             2   3   4 |
|o3 = ideal (a , b , c )|
|                       |
|o3 : Ideal of S        |
+-----------------------+

Caveat
======

If the number of elements of L differs from the number of variables in the
ring, the length of the regular sequence will be the minimum of the two.

